      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait, i'm a bit confused by your explanations. you're calling \"talos\" a root for blacksmith, but in the context of these Finnish-style words, \"talo\" usually means house. also, the way you're describing these suffixes as \"reflective\" or \"converb\" sounds a bit off for these specific forms—usually \"talossani\" is just house-in-my.\n\ncan you try to re-analyze these more traditionally? please focus strictly on the standard morphological categories (case, number, person, etc.) and the phonological rules like vowel harmony or consonant gradation that might be happening at the junctions.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
